course: dictionary
lesson: 6675
title: Obey and the clues around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To obey means to do what a person, rule or law tells you to do. «Obey the rules of the road» tells you to follow the rules when you cross or ride. Obey is a verb, so you can say obey, obeys, obeyed and obeying.
explain: Context clues help. In «The swimmers obeyed the lifeguard's whistle and climbed out», the whistle is a signal to follow, so obeyed means did what she said. Ask yourself: what did they do because someone told them to?
explain: Some sentences show the meaning through its opposite. «Strong-willed» means defiant, refusing to obey. A strong-willed child may say no to every instruction, so defiant is the opposite of obedient.
explain: Never obey someone who asks you to do something harmful or secret. If anyone tells you to keep a secret about something dangerous, do not obey them. Tell a trusted adult straight away.
fact: Obey means to do what a person, rule or law tells you to do.
fact: «Obey the rules of the road» and «obey a lifeguard's whistle» are ways to stay safe.
fact: «Kowtow» comes from Chinese for "knock head", and in English it now means being too eager to obey.
fact: «Real working dogs do not obey at once by magic»; they learn through months of training with toys, treats and praise.
fact: Objects «obey the laws of physics», which means they always behave the way those laws say they must.
exercise: «The swimmers obeyed the lifeguard's whistle and climbed out.» What does obeyed mean? | Ran away from the pool | Waved at her | Ignored her and kept swimming | *Did what she told them to do
exercise: Which of these is a safety rule you should obey? | Cross the road with your eyes shut | *Stop at the red traffic light | Ignore the safety signs at the beach | Climb over the fence to see the sea
exercise: «He is strong-willed and will not do as he is told.» What does strong-willed mean here? | *Defiant, refusing to obey | Happy to follow every order | Very tall and strong | Quiet and shy
test: Mum says, «Obey the rules of the road.» What does she want you to do? | *Follow the road rules | Eat your lunch quickly | Run across the road | Ignore the signs
test: Someone asks you to keep a secret about something dangerous. What should you do? | *Do not obey them and tell a trusted adult | Do what they say so they stay happy | Keep it secret forever | Tell only your best friend and do the dangerous thing
exam: In «Real working dogs do not obey at once by magic», what does the sentence say about how dogs learn to obey? | Dogs only obey people who are sad | *They learn through months of training with toys, treats and praise | They never learn to obey | Dogs obey by magic straight away
